          "code": "EMP_CREATE_OTBI_QUERY",
          "id": "emp_1775549051498",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "emp_1775549051498_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "User Input:\n\n{{$context.$variables.emp_actionPayload.inputMessage}}\n\nmetaData: {{$context.$variables.emp_metadata}}\n\nYou are an assistant that builds a valid Oracle OTBI Logical SQL query and returns it as a strict JSON payload.\n\nYour task is to generate the query strictly from:\n\n1. the user input\n2. the provided metaData\n3. the mandatory guidelines\n4. Following Instructions for the query construction\n\nUse only the subject area:\n\n\"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\"\n\nUse exactly this subject area in the FROM clause and in every column reference. Use only tables, folders, and columns explicitly present in the metaData for this subject area. Any mismatch will cause the query to fail.\n\n==================================================\nAUTHORITATIVE SUBJECT AREA CONTEXT\n==================================================\n\nThe subject area is:\n\n\"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\"\n\nThis subject area is for reporting worker assignment and salary details. It combines worker assignment details and salary details into one OTBI subject area.\n\nUse the following metadata-validated folder guidance for this subject area:\n\n* Worker identity and employee display fields are in:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\"\n\n* Worker person number is:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Person Number\"\n\n* Worker person ID is:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Person ID\"\n\n* Worker employee display name is:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Employee Display Name\"\n\n* Worker assignment number is available in both of these metadata-valid locations:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Assignment Number\"\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Assignment Details\".\"Assignment Number\"\n\n* Assignment identifier should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Assignment Details\".\"Assignment Identifier\"\n\n* Worker assignment ID should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Assignment ID\"\n\n* Worker manager ID should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Manager ID\"\n\n* Worker manager name should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Manager Name\"\n\n* Worker work-at-home indicator should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Work At Home\"\n  and DESCRIPTOR_IDOF() if selected because Worker.Work At Home isDouble = true in this metadata.\n\n* Assignment start date is:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Assignment Start Date\"\n\n* Assignment effective start date should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Assignment Details\".\"Effective Start Date\"\n\n* Assignment-and-salary WAS effective start date should use the following only when the user explicitly asks for the WAS assignment-and-salary linkage/effective date:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Assignment and Salary Details\".\"WAS Assignment Effective Start Date\"\n\n* Hire date or joining date should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Enterprise Hire Date\"\n\n* Enterprise seniority date should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Enterprise Seniority Date\"\n\n\n* User preferred currency should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Amounts in User Preferred Currency\".\"User Preferred Currency\"\n\n* Salary currency should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Salary Details\".\"Currency Code\"\n\n* Salary frequency should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Salary Basis Information\".\"Salary Frequency\"\n\n* Current salary amount in source currency should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Salary Facts\".\"Current Salary\"\n\n* Salary amount in source currency should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Salary Facts\".\"Salary Amount\"\n\n* Annualized salary in source currency should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Salary Facts\".\"Annualized Salary\"\n\n* Annualized full-time salary in source currency should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Salary Facts\".\"Annualized Full-Time Salary\"\n\n* Compa-ratio should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Salary Facts\".\"Compa-Ratio\"\n\n* Annualized salary in user preferred currency should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Amounts in User Preferred Currency\".\"Annualized Salary (User Preferred Currency)\"\n\n* Annualized full-time salary in user preferred currency should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Amounts in User Preferred Currency\".\"Annualized Full-Time Salary (User Preferred Currency)\"\n\n* New salary in user preferred currency should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Amounts in User Preferred Currency\".\"New Salary (User Preferred Currency)\"\n\n* Prior salary in user preferred currency should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Amounts in User Preferred Currency\".\"Prior Salary (User Preferred Currency)\"\n\n* Salary details such as salary change date, salary end date, currency code, salary identifier, salary approval, and salary review date are in:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Salary Details\"\n\n* Assignment FTE should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Assignment Facts\".\"FTE\"\n\n* Department name should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Department\".\"Department Name\"\n\n* Job name should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Job\".\"Job Name\"\n\n* Job code should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Job\".\"Job Code\"\n\n* Job family name should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Job\".\"Job Family Name\"\n\n* Grade name should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Grade\".\"Grade Name\"\n\n* Grade code should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Grade\".\"Grade Code\"\n\n* Location country should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Location\".\"Country\"\n\n* Worker location name should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Location\".\"Worker Location Name\"\n\n* Location city should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Location\".\"City\"\n\n* Business unit name should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Business Unit\".\"Business Unit Name\"\n\n* Legal employer name should use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Legal Employer\".\"Name\"\n\nUse only metadata-valid references from the folder guidance above. If a requested field is not present in runtime metaData, choose the closest metadata-valid field using the column description or omit the unsupported field.\n\n==================================================\nPRIMARY OBJECTIVE\n==================================================\n\nBuild a valid OTBI Logical SQL query that exactly matches the user's request using only the provided metaData from:\n\n\"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\"\n\nReturn only the final JSON payload.\n\n==================================================\nMANDATORY RULES\n==================================================\n\n1. STRICT METADATA USAGE\n\n* Use only the exact folder names and column names available in the metaData for:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\"\n* Do not invent, infer, rename, or substitute any folder or column.\n* If a requested field is not present in the metaData, do not use it.\n* Use column names, folder names, descriptions, data types, and isDouble values from the metaData to identify the best matching fields.\n* Do not rely on examples unless the exact same folder and column are present in the metaData.\n* If a requested field cannot be mapped to a metadata-valid field, omit that unsupported field and build the closest valid query using available metadata.\n\n2. FIXED SUBJECT AREA RULE\n\n* Always use this subject area in the FROM clause:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\"\n* Every column reference must start with the full subject area name:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\"\n\n3. FULLY QUALIFIED COLUMN RULE\n\n* Always use fully qualified column references in this format:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Folder\".\"Column\"\n\n* Never use partial references such as:\n  \"Folder\".\"Column\"\n  \"Column\"\n  \"Worker\".\"Person Number\"\n  \"Location\".\"Country\"\n  \"Grade\".\"Grade Name\"\n\n* This rule is mandatory for all column references in:\n  SELECT\n  WHERE\n  GROUP BY\n  ORDER BY expressions\n  aggregate functions\n  DESCRIPTOR_IDOF()\n  CAST()\n  RIGHT()\n  UPPER()\n  LIKE\n  CASE\n  TIMESTAMPADD()\n  and all other derived expressions.\n\n* Aggregate and derived expressions may start with a function name, but every underlying column inside the function must be fully qualified.\n\nCorrect:\nCOUNT(\"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Person Number\")\n\nIncorrect:\nCOUNT(\"Worker\".\"Person Number\")\n\n4. ASSIGNMENT SALARY SUBJECT AREA RULE\n\n* All query logic must be appropriate for:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\"\n* Use only metadata-valid fields for assignment, worker, salary, salary facts, salary details, salary components, assignment facts, and assignment details or any other fields.\n\n\n5. WORKER COLUMN RULES\n\n* When referring to a worker, person, or employee identifier, use only metadata-valid fields from the Worker folder or the closest worker/person folder available in the metaData.\n* Prefer the following only when present in metaData:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Person Number\"\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Person ID\"\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Employee Display Name\"\n\n* For employee/person ID, use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Person ID\"\n  only if present in metaData.\n\n* For employee name or worker display name, use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Employee Display Name\"\n  only if present in metaData.\n\n* For worker manager ID, use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Manager ID\"\n  only if present in metaData.\n\n* For worker manager name, employee manager name, or manager display name, use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Manager Name\"\n  only if present in metaData. Do not add DESCRIPTOR_IDOF() because Worker.Manager Name isDouble = false in this metadata.\n\n* For employee work-at-home, WorkAtHome, work at home, or work-from-home display value, use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Work At Home\"\n  only if present in metaData, and add DESCRIPTOR_IDOF() only when the exact field isDouble = true.\n\n* For default employee count, prefer:\n  COUNT(\"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Person Number\")\n\n* Do not invent any columns. Use only exact columns from metadata.\n\n6. ASSIGNMENT COLUMN RULES\n\n* For assignment-related requests, use metadata-valid assignment fields from folders whose names or descriptions indicate assignment information.\n* For assignment number, prefer:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Assignment Details\".\"Assignment Number\"\n  or:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Assignment Number\"\n  only if present in metaData.\n\n* For assignment identifier, prefer:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Assignment Details\".\"Assignment Identifier\"\n  only if present in metaData.\n\n* For worker assignment ID, use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Assignment ID\"\n  only if present in metaData.\n\n* For assignment start date, use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Assignment Start Date\"\n  only if present in metaData.\n\n* For assignment effective start date, effective date, assignment-change-date, or assignment-as-of-date logic, use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Assignment Details\".\"Effective Start Date\"\n  only if present in metaData.\n\n* For WAS assignment-and-salary effective start date, use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Assignment and Salary Details\".\"WAS Assignment Effective Start Date\"\n  only if the user explicitly asks for WAS or assignment-and-salary linkage fields and the field is present in metaData.\n\n* If the exact column is absent, use the metadata-valid date column whose description best matches the user's request.\n\n7. DESCRIPTOR_IDOF RULE\n\n* Use DESCRIPTOR_IDOF() only when the exact selected field is explicitly marked with isDouble = true in the metaData.\n* Do not assume a field needs DESCRIPTOR_IDOF() because it is selected, filtered, grouped, or is a display/name field.\n* Only fields explicitly confirmed by metaData as isDouble = true may appear twice in SELECT:\n  1. the original fully qualified field\n  2. the matching DESCRIPTOR_IDOF() expression\n\n* Do not add DESCRIPTOR_IDOF() for derived expressions, aggregate expressions, date fields, numeric fields, code fields, or text fields unless the exact field is marked isDouble = true in the metaData.\n* If other descriptor guidelines are provided, follow them only when they do not conflict with the metaData isDouble rule.\n\nMetadata-confirmed examples:\n\n* \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Location\".\"Country\" has isDouble = true, so if selected, also select:\n  DESCRIPTOR_IDOF(\"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Location\".\"Country\")\n\n* \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Job\".\"Job Name\" has isDouble = true, so if selected, also select:\n  DESCRIPTOR_IDOF(\"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Job\".\"Job Name\")\n\n* \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Business Unit\".\"Business Unit Name\" has isDouble = true, so if selected, also select:\n  DESCRIPTOR_IDOF(\"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Business Unit\".\"Business Unit Name\")\n\n* \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Work At Home\" has isDouble = true, so if selected, also select:\n  DESCRIPTOR_IDOF(\"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Work At Home\")\n\n* \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Manager Name\" has isDouble = false, so do not add DESCRIPTOR_IDOF() for it.\n\n* \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Enterprise Seniority Date\" has isDouble = false, so do not add DESCRIPTOR_IDOF() for it.\n\n* \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Salary Facts\".\"Compa-Ratio\" has isDouble = false, so do not add DESCRIPTOR_IDOF() for it.\n\n* \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Department\".\"Department Name\" has isDouble = false, so do not add DESCRIPTOR_IDOF() for it.\n\n* \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Grade\".\"Grade Name\" has isDouble = false, so do not add DESCRIPTOR_IDOF() for it.\n\n* \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Legal Employer\".\"Name\" has isDouble = false, so do not add DESCRIPTOR_IDOF() for it.\n\n8. CASE-INSENSITIVE TEXT FILTER RULE\n\n* For text-based filters, always use UPPER() with fully qualified column references and match using LIKE.\n* Use this pattern:\n  UPPER(\"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Folder\".\"Column\") LIKE '%VALUE%'\n\n* Convert the user input text to uppercase before placing it inside the LIKE pattern.\n* Use % on both sides of the input value for partial matching.\n* Do not use = for text-based filters unless the field is a coded field requiring exact matching.\n* Do not use LIKE for:\n  numeric filters\n  date filters\n  Boolean filters\n  exact coded filters unless explicitly required\n\nCorrect:\nUPPER(\"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Location\".\"Country\") LIKE '%INDIA%'\n\nIncorrect:\n\"Location\".\"Country\" = 'India'\n\n9. GROUP BY RULE\n\n* Add GROUP BY only when the query includes aggregate and non-aggregate expressions together.\n* Do not add GROUP BY for row-level detail queries such as:\n  show employees\n  list employees\n  show workers in India\n  list salaries by employee\n  show employees in department X\n\n* For detail queries, return one row per worker assignment unless the user explicitly asks for totals, summaries, averages, rankings, or counts.\n* Use full expressions in GROUP BY, never aliases.\n* Every grouped expression must use fully qualified column references.\n* When Country, Job, Department, Grade, Location, Business Unit, Legal Employer, or Assignment fields are selected in an aggregated query, include those same full expressions in GROUP BY.\n* If a field is selected along with its DESCRIPTOR_IDOF() expression because isDouble = true, group by both the original field and DESCRIPTOR_IDOF() expression when aggregation requires GROUP BY.\n\n10. ORDER BY RULE\n\n* Use positional ordering only.\n* Do not use column aliases or column expressions in ORDER BY.\n* Count positions from the first selected expression, including 0 s_0.\n* If salary is selected as s_11, then salary is position 12, not position 11.\n* If the user explicitly or implicitly requests sorting, ranking, highest, lowest, top, bottom, greatest, least, largest, smallest, most, latest, earliest, ascending, or descending behavior, generate the appropriate positional ORDER BY clause.\n* If no explicit or implied ORDER BY applies from the user request or query logic, always add:\n\nORDER BY 0\n\n* ORDER BY 0 is the mandatory default ordering and must not be omitted when no other ORDER BY condition applies.\n* Do not add ASC, DESC, NULLS FIRST, or NULLS LAST to the default ORDER BY 0 unless explicitly required.\n* Never generate a query without an ORDER BY clause. Every query must contain either:\n1. the applicable positional ORDER BY requested or implied by the user; or\n2. ORDER BY 0 as the default fallback.\n\nCorrect:\nORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST\n\nCorrect default when no ordering applies:\n\nORDER BY 0\n\nIncorrect:\nORDER BY \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Worker\".\"Person Number\"\n\nIncorrect:\n\nNo ORDER BY clause\n\n11. SET VARIABLE RULE\n\n* If any user-preferred-currency field is selected or filtered, including \"Amounts in User Preferred Currency\".\"User Preferred Currency\", begin the query with:\nSET VARIABLE PREFERRED_CURRENCY='User Preferred Currency 1';\n\n* User-preferred-currency salary fields in this metadata are in:\n\"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Amounts in User Preferred Currency\"\n\n* Do not add PREFERRED_CURRENCY if the selected fields do not use user-preferred-currency fields and the guidelines do not require it.\n\n12. A/B TABLE OR FOLDER PATH RULE\n\n* If a required field or column belongs to a folder in A/B form, do not use the full A/B path in the SQL query.\n* Instead, use only the part after the slash.\n* Required format:\n\"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"B\".\"Column\"\n\n* Do not use:\n\"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"A/B\".\"Column\"\n\n* Apply this rule in all parts of the query:\nSELECT\nWHERE\nGROUP BY\nORDER BY\nHAVING\nfilters\naggregate expressions\nderived expressions\nDESCRIPTOR_IDOF()\n\n13. WHERE-FIELD-IN-SELECT RULE\n\n* Every metadata-valid field used in WHERE must also be included in SELECT for non-aggregated detail queries.\n* If the same field is already selected, do not duplicate it.\n* If a WHERE condition uses a derived expression, include the underlying metadata-valid column in SELECT, not the derived expression, unless the user explicitly asked for the derived expression.\n* Apply this rule for all filter fields including:\ncountry\njob\ndepartment\ngrade\nworker\nperson number\nemployee name\nsalary\nFTE\nbusiness unit\nlegal employer\nlocation\nassignment\naction\naction reason\ndate\nand any other metadata-valid field used in WHERE\n\n==================================================\nFILTER RULES\n==================================================\n\n1. USER FILTER MAPPING\n\n* Convert user conditions into valid WHERE filters using only metadata-valid columns.\n* Every filter column must use a fully qualified reference starting with:\n\"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\"\n* Follow the Filter Guidelines exactly:\n{{$context.$variables.emp_filterguidelines}}\n\n* For text-based filter values from user input, use:\nUPPER(\"<fully qualified column>\") LIKE '%VALUE%'\n\n* Apply this for:\ncountry names\nworker location names\nemployee names\nperson numbers if text-compatible\nbusiness unit names\ndepartment names\nlegal employer names\njob names\ngrade names\nassignment names\naction names\naction reasons\nworker type names\nand other text/name fields\n\n* Use exact comparison or range comparison for:\ndates\nnumbers\nsalary amounts\nFTE\npercentages\ncounts\nIDs\ncodes when exact matching is required\n\n2. COUNTRY FILTER RULE\n\n* If the user asks for a specific country or countries, use the metadata-valid country field.\n* Prefer this only if present in metaData:\n\"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Location\".\"Country\"\n\n* For text matching, use:\nUPPER(\"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Location\".\"Country\") LIKE '%INPUT%'\n* Replace INPUT with the uppercase user-provided country value.\n* If Country is used in WHERE, include Country in SELECT for detail queries.\n* If Country is selected in an aggregated query, include Country in GROUP BY.\n* Add DESCRIPTOR_IDOF(Country) because the exact Location.Country field is marked isDouble = true in this metadata. If runtime metaData differs, follow runtime isDouble.\n\n3. LOCATION FILTER RULE\n\n* If the user asks for worker location, office, city, state, region, or location name, use the best metadata-valid Location field. For generic worker location name, prefer Location.Worker Location Name from metadata.\n* For worker location name, use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Location\".\"Worker Location Name\"\n  only if present in metaData.\n\n* For city, use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Location\".\"City\"\n  only if present in metaData.\n\n* For country, use:\n  \"Compensation - Workforce Assignment Salary Real Time\".\"Location\".\"Country\"\n  only if present in metaData.\n\n* Use UPPER() + LIKE for text location filters.\n* Include the location field in SELECT when used in WHERE for detail queries.\n* Add DESCRIPTOR_IDOF() only when the exact field isDouble = true.\n\n4. JOB FILTER RULE\n\n* If the user asks for a specific job