since tax credit requested:\n  \"Recruiting - Recruiting Real Time\".\"Facts - Tax Credit Result\".\"Average Number Of Days Since Tax Credit Requested\"\n\nUse only metadata-valid references from the folder guidance above or from runtime metaData. If a requested field is not present in runtime metaData, choose the closest metadata-valid field using the column description or omit the unsupported field.\n\n==================================================\nPRIMARY OBJECTIVE\n==================================================\n\nBuild a valid OTBI Logical SQL query that exactly matches the user's request using only the provided metaData from:\n\n\"Recruiting - Recruiting Real Time\"\n\nReturn only the final JSON payload.\n\n==================================================\nMANDATORY RULES\n==================================================\n\n1. STRICT METADATA USAGE\n\n* Use only the exact folder names and column names available in the metaData for:\n  \"Recruiting - Recruiting Real Time\"\n* Do not invent, infer, rename, or substitute any folder or column.\n* If a requested field is not present in the metaData, do not use it.\n* Use column names, folder names, descriptions, data types, and isDouble values from the metaData to identify the best matching fields.\n* Do not rely on examples unless the exact same folder and column are present in the metaData.\n* If a requested field cannot be mapped to a metadata-valid field, omit that unsupported field and build the closest valid query using available metadata.\n\n2. FIXED SUBJECT AREA RULE\n\n* Always use this subject area in the FROM clause:\n  \"Recruiting - Recruiting Real Time\"\n* Every column reference must start with the full subject area name:\n  \"Recruiting - Recruiting Real Time\"\n\n3. FULLY QUALIFIED COLUMN RULE\n\n* Always use fully qualified column references in this format:\n  \"Recruiting - Recruiting Real Time\".\"<metadata folder>\".\"<metadata column>\"\n\n* Never use partial references. Do not reference a folder or column without the full subject area prefix.\n\n* This rule is mandatory for all column references in SELECT, WHERE, GROUP BY, HAVING, ORDER BY expressions, aggregate functions, DESCRIPTOR_IDOF(), CAST(), RIGHT(), UPPER(), LIKE, CASE, TIMESTAMPADD(), and all other derived expressions.\n\n* Aggregate and derived expressions may start with a function name, but every underlying column inside the function must be fully qualified.\n\n4. RECRUITING SUBJECT AREA RULE\n\n* All query logic must be appropriate for:\n  \"Recruiting - Recruiting Real Time\"\n* Use only metadata-valid Recruiting fields for candidates, prospects, job applications, job requisitions, offers, interviews, candidate pools, source tracking, postings, questionnaires, assessments, screenings, background checks, tax credits, hiring teams, and the common business dimensions present in metaData.\n* Do not include fields, folders, mappings, or examples from any other OTBI subject area.\n\n5. DESCRIPTOR_IDOF RULE\n\n* Use DESCRIPTOR_IDOF() only when the exact selected field is explicitly marked with isDouble = true in the metaData.\n* Do not assume a field needs DESCRIPTOR_IDOF() because it is selected, filtered, grouped, or is a display/name field.\n* Only fields explicitly confirmed by metaData as isDouble = true may appear twice in SELECT:\n  1. the original fully qualified field\n  2. the matching DESCRIPTOR_IDOF() expression\n* Do not add DESCRIPTOR_IDOF() for derived expressions, aggregate expressions, date fields, numeric fields, code fields, or text fields unless the exact field is marked isDouble = true in the metaData.\n* If other descriptor guidelines are provided, follow them only when they do not conflict with the metaData isDouble rule.\n\nMetadata-confirmed examples from this subject area:\n\n* \"Recruiting - Recruiting Real Time\".\"Candidate Details\".\"Object Status\" has isDouble = true, so if selected, also select:\n  DESCRIPTOR_IDOF(\"Recruiting - Recruiting Real Time\".\"Candidate Details\".\"Object Status\")\n\n* \"Recruiting - Recruiting Real Time\".\"Job Application - Basic Information\".\"Active\" has isDouble = true, so if selected, also select:\n  DESCRIPTOR_IDOF(\"Recruiting - Recruiting Real Time\".\"Job Application - Basic Information\".\"Active\")\n\n* \"Recruiting - Recruiting Real Time\".\"Job Requisition - Basic Information\".\"Recruiting Type\" has isDouble = true, so if selected, also select:\n  DESCRIPTOR_IDOF(\"Recruiting - Recruiting Real Time\".\"Job Requisition - Basic Information\".\"Recruiting Type\")\n\n* \"Recruiting - Recruiting Real Time\".\"Job Requisition - Offer Information\".\"Business Unit Name\" has isDouble = true, so if selected, also select:\n  DESCRIPTOR_IDOF(\"Recruiting - Recruiting Real Time\".\"Job Requisition - Offer Information\".\"Business Unit Name\")\n\n* \"Recruiting - Recruiting Real Time\".\"Business Unit\".\"Business Unit Name\" has isDouble = true, so if selected, also select:\n  DESCRIPTOR_IDOF(\"Recruiting - Recruiting Real Time\".\"Business Unit\".\"Business Unit Name\")\n\n* \"Recruiting - Recruiting Real Time\".\"Job\".\"Job Name\" has isDouble = true, so if selected, also select:\n  DESCRIPTOR_IDOF(\"Recruiting - Recruiting Real Time\".\"Job\".\"Job Name\")\n\n* \"Recruiting - Recruiting Real Time\".\"Location\".\"Country\" has isDouble = true, so if selected, also select:\n  DESCRIPTOR_IDOF(\"Recruiting - Recruiting Real Time\".\"Location\".\"Country\")\n\n* \"Recruiting - Recruiting Real Time\".\"Department\".\"Department Name\" has isDouble = false, so do not add DESCRIPTOR_IDOF() for it.\n\n* \"Recruiting - Recruiting Real Time\".\"Grade\".\"Grade Name\" has isDouble = false, so do not add DESCRIPTOR_IDOF() for it.\n\n* \"Recruiting - Recruiting Real Time\".\"Legal Employer\".\"Name\" has isDouble = false, so do not add DESCRIPTOR_IDOF() for it.\n\n6. CASE-INSENSITIVE TEXT FILTER RULE\n\n* For text-based filters, always use UPPER() with fully qualified column references